WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.497 --> 00:00:02.844
Hello Fandango MOVIECLIPS, we are the Paz Brothers

00:00:02.845 --> 00:00:05.700
directors of the biblical apocalypse film 'Jeruzalem'. 

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.900
To get your primed and ready to check out 'Jeruzalem'

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:11.400
We're going to give you are top five favorite religious horror movies. 

00:00:11.401 --> 00:00:14.600
Number five on the list is 2009's 'Drag Me To Hell'. 

00:00:14.563 --> 00:00:16.370
An old woman curses Christine

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.599
Who must figure out how to rid herself of the demons that haunt her. 

00:00:19.615 --> 00:00:23.000
Directed by Sam Raimi, the mastermind behind the Evil Dead films;

00:00:23.001 --> 00:00:25.589
and written by Sam and his brother Ivan

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.609
The fourth film on our list is
[REC].

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.599
With a perfect blend of both style
and substance,

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:34.600
directors Jaume Balaguero and Paco Plaza set out to create a classic horror movie,

00:00:34.046 --> 00:00:36.220
 but to tell the story more like a TV show.

00:00:36.221 --> 00:00:39.220
[REC] unfolds in real-time and
attempts to immerse the viewer in the experience

00:00:39.677 --> 00:00:43.335
through the eyes of a TV reporter and her cameraman.

00:00:43.336 --> 00:00:46.220
The production is sparse with an almost claustrophobic feel

00:00:46.221 --> 00:00:48.220
where something horrifying and unknown is happening.

00:00:48.221 --> 00:00:50.220
Number three is The Devil’s
Advocate.

00:00:50.221 --> 00:00:54.800
We're talking about director Guy Green’s 1977 West German English-language film,

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:57.500
not the Keanu Reeves/Al Pacino film of the same name.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:01:00.500
'The Devil’s Advocate' tells the story of a Roman Catholic priest

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:03.773
The priest is sent to a remote Italian village to play devil’s advocate

00:01:03.774 --> 00:01:08.500
in the investigation of a man who is a candidate to be canonized by the church.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:12.000
At number two we have Roman Polanski’s classic psychological horror film 

00:01:12.001 --> 00:01:13.185
'Rosemary’s Baby'. 

00:01:13.186 --> 00:01:16.400
Centering around Rosemary Woodhouse, a young housewife who,

00:01:16.401 --> 00:01:21.100
along with her husband, moves into a fancy apartment building where strange things begin to happen

00:01:21.101 --> 00:01:24.100
When she wakes with scratch marks all over her body

00:01:24.101 --> 00:01:27.500
and soon receives news that she is pregnant, things take a decidedly evil turn.

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:29.500
Which brings us to number one on our list.

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:33.340
It’s The Exorcist. William Friedken’s 1973 masterpiece

00:01:33.341 --> 00:01:37.900
that was the first horror film to be nominated for the Best Picture Academy Award.

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:41.775
The head-turning, vomit-spewing, demonically possessed 12-year-old girl

00:01:41.776 --> 00:01:44.890
ith a serious potty mouth is pretty much Hollywood’s gold standard

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:45.890
for evil personified.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:49.500
And there you have it, our Top Five favorite religious-horror movies.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:53.000
And that should be perfect to get you ready to check out our film, 'Jeruzalem'.

00:01:53.001 --> 00:01:56.100
It tells the story of two young American women who travel to Tel Aviv 

00:01:56.101 --> 00:01:59.900
for a vacation, but are persuaded to change their plans by a young archeologist.

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:01.600
And pretty soon, all hell breaks loose

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:04.700
and they find themselves in the middle of a biblical apocalypse.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:08.600
I’m Yoav and this is my brother Doron for Fandango Movieclips.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:12.600
Be sure to check out 'Jeruzalem' in theaters now.

